E027: SPEEDRUN_VERB_IMAGES=1: an image verb's name is "#" and a hash of the image it shows

An inventory slot is an image verb. Its id, mode and place are the same whatever object it shows, and it has no
text, so a state dump could not tell one page of the inventory from the next. With the switch, verbText() gives an
image verb the FNV-1a hash of its rtVerb resource (the object image setVerbObject() copied there) as its name. No
pixel and no game text leaves the process. Off (the default): no name, as before.

On top of patches 0001-0010 (the tree of svm-e024); the engine built with it is svm-e027.

--- a/engines/scumm/speedrun/speedrun_bridge.cpp
+++ b/engines/scumm/speedrun/speedrun_bridge.cpp
